<repaired_code>
def find_roots(
    graph: "Graph", prop: "URIRef", roots: Optional[Set["Node"]] = None
) -> Set["Node"]:
    # Get all nodes that appear as subjects or objects in triples with the given property
    all_nodes = set()
    non_roots = set()
    
    # Find all subject-object pairs for the given property
    for subject, object in graph.subject_objects(prop):
        all_nodes.add(subject)
        all_nodes.add(object)
        # Any node that appears as an object (child) is not a root
        non_roots.add(subject)
    
    # If roots parameter is provided, restrict to those nodes
    if roots is not None:
        all_nodes.intersection_update(roots)
    
    # Roots are nodes that never appear as subjects in the hierarchy
    return all_nodes - non_roots
</repaired_code>

This implementation:
1. Creates sets to track all nodes and non-root nodes
2. Uses graph.subject_objects() to iterate through all triples with the given property
3. Identifies nodes that appear as subjects (children) in the hierarchy as non-roots
4. Handles the optional roots parameter by restricting the search if provided
5. Returns the set difference between all nodes and non-roots to find the root nodes

The code now properly implements the root-finding functionality described in the docstring, handling the hierarchical relationship (child, prop, parent) correctly.

